- Problem statement: Monocarp has a regular bracket sequence of length n (n is even). He wants to restore his RBS by placing brackets on the odd positions. However, due to data corruption, only characters on even positions remain. The goal is to choose one RBS with minimum cost.
- Input:
  - The first line contains a single integer t (1≤t≤5000) — the number of test cases.
  - Next t cases follow.
  - The first line of each test case contains a single integer n (2≤n≤2⋅105; n is even) — the length of string s.
  - The second line of each test case contains a string s of length n, where all characters on the odd positions are '_' and all characters on the even positions are either '(' or ')'.
- Constraints: s can be restored to at least one regular bracket sequence; the total sum of n over all test cases doesn't exceed 2⋅105.
- Output: For each test case, print one integer — the minimum cost of the regular bracket sequence that can be obtained from s by replacing '_'-s with brackets.
